       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problems are still there.\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg. It could seriously harm the patient.\n- **The confirmation isn't from a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so you can't verify that this dose is intended for the patient.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Have the prescribing clinician review the order. If 1000 mg was a typo, they can give me the correct dose. If they really intend a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves. That way it goes through pharmacy verification and the hospital's safety checks.\n- If you think a patient may already have received a dose like this, tell the clinical team or pharmacy right away.\n\nIf a clinician gives me a dose within the standard range, I'll enter it."
